<https://benchmarks.rewire.it/id/discovery-benchmark-cami> <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab#profile> "{\"coverage\":\"reviewed\",\"diagram\":{\"caption\":\"Conceptual procedure. Task variants and protocol versions retain their separate scoring conditions.\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\",\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations; Methods: Challenge datasets, Challenge organization, Evaluation metrics; Figures 2–4; Table 1; Methods: Evaluation metrics; Table 1\",\"steps\":[\"Allowed inputs: Released sequence data and track-specific reference resources.\",\"Splits: CAMI II supplied public-genome practice datasets with ground truth before its blinded challenge. Challenge datasets were marine, strain-madness and plant-associated communities; these are challenge conditions, not a standard supervised train/validation/test partition.\",\"Metrics: Assembly: genome fraction, NGA50, mismatches, misassemblies and strain precision/recall. Genome binning: purity, completeness, ARI and binned fraction. Taxonomic binning: purity, completeness, F1 and accuracy. Profiling: identification, abundance and diversity metrics, including L1, Bray–Curtis and weighted UniFrac.\"],\"title\":\"Evaluation procedure\"},\"facts\":[{\"label\":\"Datasets\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Challenge-specific metagenomic datasets, including a longitudinal human-gut collection in CAMI III.\"},{\"label\":\"Splits\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Methods: Challenge datasets, Challenge organization, Evaluation metrics; Figures 2–4; Table 1\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"CAMI II supplied public-genome practice datasets with ground truth before its blinded challenge. Challenge datasets were marine, strain-madness and plant-associated communities; these are challenge conditions, not a standard supervised train/validation/test partition.\"},{\"label\":\"Metrics\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Methods: Evaluation metrics; Table 1\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Assembly: genome fraction, NGA50, mismatches, misassemblies and strain precision/recall. Genome binning: purity, completeness, ARI and binned fraction. Taxonomic binning: purity, completeness, F1 and accuracy. Profiling: identification, abundance and diversity metrics, including L1, Bray–Curtis and weighted UniFrac.\"},{\"label\":\"Baselines\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Methods: Challenge datasets, Challenge organization, Evaluation metrics; Figures 2–4; Table 1\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Submitted programs are compared under the same data condition. Gold-standard assemblies and MEGAHIT assemblies separate binning performance from upstream assembly error; published method identities and versions are listed in Table 1.\"},{\"label\":\"Leakage controls\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Methods: Challenge datasets, Challenge organization, Evaluation metrics; Figures 2–4; Table 1\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Challenge genome data and metadata were kept confidential until the challenge ended. Public reference collections dated 8 January 2019 were supplied for reference-based methods. CAMI II also includes public genomes, so novelty is stratified rather than assumed for every organism.\"},{\"label\":\"Uncertainty\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Figure 3 and Figure 4 captions: standard error across taxonomic bins versus standard deviation across samples\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Uncertainty is task-specific: taxonomic binning Figure 3 uses standard errors across bins; taxonomic profiling Figure 4 reports means across samples with standard deviations. These are not a common seed-based interval for every CAMI metric.\"},{\"label\":\"Entity type\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Metagenomic community challenge series.\"},{\"label\":\"Organisms\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Microbial communities; CAMI III includes longitudinal human-gut samples.\"},{\"label\":\"Assays\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Challenge-specific metagenomic sequence data and reference composition.\"},{\"label\":\"Allowed inputs\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Released sequence data and track-specific reference resources.\"},{\"label\":\"Adaptation\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"status\":\"source_checked\",\"value\":\"Methods process challenge inputs; a challenge edition and track determine resource rules.\"}],\"gaps\":[],\"limitations\":[{\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Methods: Challenge datasets, Challenge organization, Evaluation metrics; Figures 2–4; Table 1\",\"text\":\"This profile documents CAMI II as a concrete protocol example. Other CAMI rounds may use different genomes, reference databases and metrics; strain diversity and input assembly quality materially change the task.\"}],\"review\":{\"date\":\"2026-09-16\",\"method\":\"automated_source_review\",\"note\":\"Primary paper and/or task implementation reviewed for the explicitly cited methodology claims. Scope-limited absence is recorded only after the documented source search; no model runs or independent reproduction. Independent automated spot review corrected interval terminology and sequence-identity scope against the original figure captions and methods.\"},\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"CAMI is a series of blinded metagenomic software challenges. In CAMI II, participants received simulated short and long reads from defined communities and submitted assemblies, genome bins, taxonomic assignments or abundance profiles. Reference truth was used only for scoring, and software versions, input read types and community conditions were kept distinct.\",\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-discovery-final-cami2\"],\"source_locator\":\"Methods: Challenge datasets, Challenge organization, Evaluation metrics; Figures 2–4; Table 1\",\"title\":\"Evaluation methodology\"}],\"strengths\":[{\"source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\",\"text\":\"Multiple tracks distinguish assembly, binning and abundance estimation.\"}],\"summary\":\"CAMI is a community benchmark program for metagenomic computational methods.\",\"summary_source_ids\":[\"evidence-benchmark-cami-snapshot\"],\"summary_source_locator\":\"Official CAMI homepage: initiative description; challenges; dataset correction notices; toolkit citations\"}"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#JSON> <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/graph/asserted> .
<https://benchmarks.rewire.it/id/discovery-benchmark-cami> <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/vocab#runDocumentation> "{\"record_id\":\"discovery-benchmark-cami\",\"source_ids\":[\"run-doc-cami-official-20260917\"],\"source_locator\":\"Official portal: Resources, Submit, Software and File formats links\",\"status\":\"official_documentation_linked\",\"summary\":\"Official portal links task-specific datasets, formats, evaluation software and a submission tutorial. Choose assembly, binning or taxonomic profiling plus a specific data release first; there is no single command for all CAMI tracks. This website snapshot does not pin the linked evaluators.\"}"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#JSON> <https://benchmarks.rewire.it/graph/asserted> .
